class.description:
[CSVReader] reads a CSV file ([url=https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4180]RFC 4180[/url], UTF-8) from a file buffer, one row at a time. Memory use is one row and a 64 KiB buffer, not the size of the file, so it suits files that are too large for [CSV], which holds every cell in memory. The syntax is the same as in [CSV]: quoted cells may contain the delimiter, double quotes ([code]""[/code]) and line breaks, blank lines are skipped and a byte order mark is ignored. The delimiter and the header row come from [SerializerOptions] ([member SerializerOptions.csv_delimiter], [member SerializerOptions.csv_headers]); the delimiter must be an ASCII character. Rows are [PackedStringArray]s of text, there is no type guessing.
Rows are read in order with [method read_row] or [method read_rows]. [method seek_row] jumps to a row number, for example to show one page of a table: the reader remembers the file position of every 1024th row it has passed, so a jump reads at most 1024 rows after the nearest known position. [method count_rows] reads the whole file once to count the rows, on the calling thread (a full scan for a large file). Rows are counted in an [int]: files are limited to 2^31 rows. Equal column names in the header: [method read_record] keeps the last one.
The file is read through [FileAccess], so [code]res://[/code], [code]user://[/code] and packed files work on every platform, including the Web export. Nothing is read in a thread.
If a row is invalid (a quoted cell that is not closed, or more cells than the header has columns), the reader stops: [method get_error] returns the error, the read methods return empty results, and [method seek_row] clears the error. Rows before the error are read normally.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var reader = CSVReader.open("user://big.csv")
print(reader.get_header()) # ["name", "level"]
while true:
	var row = reader.read_row()
	if row.is_empty():
		break # The end of the file, or an error: see reader.get_error().
	print(row[0])

# One page of 50 rows, starting at row 100000.
reader.seek_row(100000)
var page = reader.read_rows(50)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var reader = CsvReader.Open("user://big.csv");
GD.Print(reader.GetHeader()); // ["name", "level"]
while (true)
{
	var row = reader.ReadRow();
	if (row.Length == 0)
	{
		break; // The end of the file, or an error: see reader.GetError().
	}
	GD.Print(row[0]);
}

// One page of 50 rows, starting at row 100000.
reader.SeekRow(100000);
var page = reader.ReadRows(50);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] A [CSVReader] should be used by one thread at a time.
